#
# Semantic content of the header page: values, relations and properties.
# The presence of each name and type comes with the Tier 0 generator.

assertion  XBD.time.h.001
anchor     basedefs/time.h.html#DESCRIPTION/CLOCKS_PER_SEC
class      required
since      1988
says       CLOCKS_PER_SEC is an expression of type clock_t and is positive.
test       t/001-clocks-per-sec.c
nomutant   run-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.time.h.002
anchor     basedefs/time.h.html#DESCRIPTION/CLOCKS_PER_SEC
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1988
says       On an XSI system CLOCKS_PER_SEC is one million.
test       t/002-clocks-per-sec-xsi.c
nomutant   run-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.time.h.003
anchor     basedefs/time.h.html#DESCRIPTION/TIME_UTC
class      required
since      2024
says       TIME_UTC is an integer constant greater than zero that can be used in
           #if.
test       t/003-time-utc.c
nomutant   compile-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.time.h.004
anchor     basedefs/time.h.html#DESCRIPTION/CLOCK_MONOTONIC
class      required
since      2024
says       CLOCK_REALTIME and CLOCK_MONOTONIC (and CLOCK_PROCESS_CPUTIME_ID and
           CLOCK_THREAD_CPUTIME_ID where defined) can be held in a clockid_t and
           name different clocks, so their values differ.
note       The page does not say the identifiers differ in words; they name
           clocks of different kinds (clock_settime() must set the real-time
           clock and must fail for the monotonic clock, XSH clock_settime
           DESCRIPTION and ERRORS), so one value for those two is not possible;
           the CPU-time clocks measure other quantities.
           CLOCK_PROCESS_CPUTIME_ID and CLOCK_THREAD_CPUTIME_ID exist only with
           the CPU-time options.
           See Q-168 in docs/standard-issues.md.
test       t/004-clock-ids.c
nomutant   run-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.time.h.005
anchor     basedefs/time.h.html#DESCRIPTION/tm
class      required
since      1988
says       The members of the structure gmtime(), gmtime_r(), localtime() and
           localtime_r() fill in lie in the ranges the page gives (seconds 0 to
           60, minutes 0 to 59, hours 0 to 23, day of month 1 to 31, month 0 to
           11, weekday 0 to 6, day of year 0 to 365), and tm_isdst is never
           negative.
note       tm_isdst is "positive if Daylight Saving Time is in effect and 0 if
           not"; a negative value is forbidden for results of the interfaces.
test       t/005-tm-ranges.c
nomutant   run-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.time.h.006
anchor     basedefs/time.h.html#DESCRIPTION/timespec
class      required
since      2024
says       The tv_nsec member of a timespec filled in by clock_gettime(),
           clock_getres() or timespec_get() is between 0 and 999999999.
test       t/006-timespec-nsec.c
nomutant   run-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.time.h.007
anchor     basedefs/time.h.html#DESCRIPTION/getdate_err
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1988
says       On an XSI system <time.h> provides getdate_err as an expression of
           type int.
test       t/007-getdate-err.c
nomutant   compile-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants
